[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/comments/254740709","html_url":"https://github.com/graphql/graphql-js/issues/522#issuecomment-254740709","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/522","id":254740709,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI1NDc0MDcwOQ==","user":{"login":"stubailo","id":448783,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0ODc4Mw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/448783?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stubailo","html_url":"https://github.com/stubailo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stubailo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stubailo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stubailo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stubailo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stubailo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stubailo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stubailo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stubailo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stubailo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-10-19T07:54:56Z","updated_at":"2016-10-19T07:54:56Z","body":"I don't have an opinion on the underlying issue, but you can work around this limitation by using an alias in the query.\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/comments/254740709/reactions","total_count":8,"+1":6,"-1":2,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/comments/254999225","html_url":"https://github.com/graphql/graphql-js/issues/522#issuecomment-254999225","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/522","id":254999225,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI1NDk5OTIyNQ==","user":{"login":"TomMcQuarrieOTH","id":21348503,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzQ4NTAz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21348503?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TomMcQuarrieOTH","html_url":"https://github.com/TomMcQuarrieOTH","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TomMcQuarrieOTH/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TomMcQuarrieOTH/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TomMcQuarrieOTH/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TomMcQuarrieOTH/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TomMcQuarrieOTH/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TomMcQuarrieOTH/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TomMcQuarrieOTH/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TomMcQuarrieOTH/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TomMcQuarrieOTH/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-10-20T03:20:57Z","updated_at":"2016-10-20T03:21:27Z","body":"Thanks @stubailo. Aliases proved to be a valid workaround, although they did add some complexities to our tests. For those playing at home, the alias is added to the query as follows:\n\n```\n        recurrence {\n          type,\n          ... on MonthlyRecurrence {\n            specificRecurrenceDate\n            monthlyRecurOn: recurOn\n          }\n          ... on FortnightlyRecurrence {\n            fortnightlyRecurOn: recurOn\n          }\n        }\n```\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/comments/254999225/reactions","total_count":11,"+1":11,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/comments/255837127","html_url":"https://github.com/graphql/graphql-js/issues/522#issuecomment-255837127","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/522","id":255837127,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI1NTgzNzEyNw==","user":{"login":"leebyron","id":50130,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwMTMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50130?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leebyron","html_url":"https://github.com/leebyron","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leebyron/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leebyron/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leebyron/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leebyron/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leebyron/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leebyron/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leebyron/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leebyron/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leebyron/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-10-24T19:14:47Z","updated_at":"2016-10-24T19:14:47Z","body":"The safe divergence case was fixed long ago, so unless you're using a very old version of graphql-js, then that case is being accounted for!\n\nLooking at this example, I would not expect this to be a safe divergence though. Perhaps it doesn't matter for your particular environment if you're using dynamically typed languages, but if you were using a statically typed language, then you would have encountered a problem when trying to correctly type the result of `recurrence.recurOn`. If one of two different Enums could be used, then your client couldn't be sure of what values would appear.\n\nIn this case you have two options:\n1. Do what @stubailo suggested, and alias one or both fields to remove the type conflict.\n2. have both `recurOn` return the same Enum on the server (combine the possible values). That might make it less clear what the possible values are for the specific `MonthlyRecurrence` case vs all possible cases, however this query usage makes it seem like differentiating the cases might not matter since the client wishes to use them in a combined way.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/comments/255837127/reactions","total_count":12,"+1":0,"-1":2,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":10,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/comments/363077863","html_url":"https://github.com/graphql/graphql-js/issues/522#issuecomment-363077863","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/522","id":363077863,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM2MzA3Nzg2Mw==","user":{"login":"brabeji","id":2237954,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMzc5NTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2237954?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeji","html_url":"https://github.com/brabeji","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeji/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeji/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeji/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeji/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeji/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeji/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeji/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeji/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeji/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2018-02-05T13:00:35Z","updated_at":"2018-02-05T16:27:05Z","body":"@leebyron There seems to be slight inconsistency. I believe these test cases are up to the spec:\r\nhttps://github.com/brabeji/graphql-js/commit/da34fd851ab7689ce7914ea04814ad47f82d5d22\r\n\r\nBut I can't wrap my head around how the argument about strongly typed languages doesn't apply to object types. How is that different from enums? Obviously, I would like the case with enums to also be safe. 😇 \r\n\r\nI know I'm very late to the party but thank you very much for any explanation.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/comments/363077863/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/comments/363253934","html_url":"https://github.com/graphql/graphql-js/issues/522#issuecomment-363253934","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/522","id":363253934,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM2MzI1MzkzNA==","user":{"login":"IvanGoncharov","id":8336157,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzMzYxNTc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8336157?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/IvanGoncharov","html_url":"https://github.com/IvanGoncharov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IvanGoncharov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IvanGoncharov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IvanGoncharov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IvanGoncharov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IvanGoncharov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IvanGoncharov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IvanGoncharov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IvanGoncharov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IvanGoncharov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2018-02-05T23:14:58Z","updated_at":"2018-02-05T23:14:58Z","body":"> But I can't wrap my head around how the argument about strongly typed languages doesn't apply to object types.\r\n\r\n@brabeji Query results are strongly typed based on possible field values: \r\nhttp://facebook.github.io/graphql/draft/#sec-Field-Selection-Merging\r\n\r\nTL;DR; Only field values are conflicting with each other. In your test case:\r\n```graphql\r\n             ... on Character {\r\n               name\r\n             }\r\n             ... on Human {\r\n               rankObject { __typename name }\r\n             }\r\n             ... on Droid {\r\n               rankObject { __typename name }\r\n             }\r\n```\r\nYou can think as it stong-typed with following unnamed type:\r\n```\r\n{\r\n   name: String\r\n   rankObject: {\r\n      name: String\r\n      __typename: String\r\n   }\r\n}\r\n```\r\nIn you enum test case you can think as it stong-typed with:\r\n```\r\n{\r\n  rank: HumanRank\r\n  rank: DroidRank #Conflict here\r\n}\r\n```","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/comments/363253934/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/comments/366786501","html_url":"https://github.com/graphql/graphql-js/issues/522#issuecomment-366786501","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/522","id":366786501,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM2Njc4NjUwMQ==","user":{"login":"brabeji","id":2237954,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMzc5NTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2237954?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeji","html_url":"https://github.com/brabeji","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeji/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeji/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeji/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeji/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeji/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeji/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeji/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeji/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeji/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2018-02-19T19:41:44Z","updated_at":"2018-02-19T19:45:26Z","body":"Btw I've just found that a very nice explanation is given in the reference code itself:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/graphql/graphql-js/blob/5fe39262a308df944a87cc85b225228e7556aaa4/src/validation/rules/OverlappingFieldsCanBeMerged.js#L665\r\n\r\n`rankObject` being a composite type \r\n> Composite types are ignored as their individual field types will be compared later recursively.\r\n\r\nand \r\n\r\n`rank` being a leaf type.\r\nhttps://github.com/graphql/graphql-js/blob/5fe39262a308df944a87cc85b225228e7556aaa4/src/validation/rules/OverlappingFieldsCanBeMerged.js#L688\r\n\r\nthank you @IvanGoncharov !","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/comments/366786501/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]